{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":28279091,"ns":0,"title":"Polemon christyi","revisions":[{"revid":1355030157,"parentid":1267937720,"minor":true,"timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:01:54Z","size":6787,"sha1":"c7dd2507f5acedacec5fc5a76b5ec2c1e62cd84b","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Short description|Species of snake}}\n{{Speciesbox\n | status = LC\n | status_system = IUCN3.1\n | status_ref = <ref name=iucn>[[species:Philipp Wagner (Biologe)|Wagner P]], [[species:Ignas Safari|Safari I]], [[species:Jumapili Chenga|Chenga J]] (2021). \"''Polemon christyi'' \". The [[IUCN]] Red List of Threatened Species 2021: https://dx.doi.org/10.2305/IUCN.UK.2021-2.RLTS.T13264526A13264534.en. Accessed on 24 February 2022.</ref>\n | genus = Polemon\n | species = christyi\n | authority = ([[George Albert Boulenger|Boulenger]], 1903)\n | synonyms  = *''Miodon christyi'' <br/>{{small|Boulenger, 1903}}\n*''Miodon unicolor'' <br/>{{small|[[Karl Patterson Schmidt|K.P. Schmidt]], 1923}}\n*''Melanocalamus leopoldi'' <br/>{{small|[[Gaston-François de Witte|de Witte]], 1941}}\n*''Miodon collaris christyi'' <br/>{{small|— [[Arthur Loveridge|Loveridge]], 1957}}\n*''Polemon christyi'' <br/>{{small|— [[Donald George Broadley|Broadley]] & [[species:Kim Monroe Howell|Howell]], 1991}}\n | synonyms_ref =<ref name=RDB/>\n}}\n\n'''''Polemon christyi''''', also known [[Common name|commonly]] as '''Christy's snake-eater''' and the '''eastern snake-eater''', is a [[species]] of mildly [[venomous]] [[Opisthoglyphous|rear-fanged]] [[snake]] in the [[subfamily]] [[Aparallactinae]] of the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Atractaspididae]]. The species is native to [[Central Africa]] and [[East Africa]].<ref name=RDB>{{NRDB species|genus=Polemon|species=christyi|accessdate=25 February 2019}}</ref><ref name=\"Portillo et al. 2019\"/>\n\n==Etymology==\nThe [[Specific name (zoology)|specific name]], ''christyi'', is in honor of English physician [[Cuthbert Christy]], who presented the [[Holotype|type specimen]] to the [[British Museum (Natural History)]].<ref name=Blgr1903>[[George Albert Boulenger|Boulenger GA]] (1903). \"Descriptions of new Snakes in the Collection of the British Museum\". ''Annals and Magazine of Natural History, Seventh Series'' '''12''': 350–354. (''Miodon christyi'', new species, p. 354).</ref><ref name=EDR>[[species:Bo Beolens|Beolens, Bo]]; [[species:Michael Watkins|Watkins, Michael]]; [[species:Michael Grayson|Grayson, Michael]] (2011). ''The Eponym Dictionary of Reptiles''. Baltimore: Johns Hopkins University Press. xiii + 296 pp. {{ISBN|978-1-4214-0135-5}}. (''Polemon christyi'', p. 54; ''P. leopoldi'', p. 155).</ref> The synonym, \"''leopoldi'' \", is in honor of [[Leopold III of Belgium|Leopold III, King of the Belgians]].<ref name=EDR/>\n\n==Geographic range==\nDistribution of ''Polemon christyi'' include [[Uganda]], the [[Democratic Republic of the Congo]],  [[South Sudan]], and western [[Kenya]]. The status of observations from [[Rwanda]] and [[Malawi]] is uncertain, whereas observations from [[Tanzania]], [[Zambia]], and possibly [[Burundi]] likely refer to ''[[Polemon ater]]'' described in 2019.<ref name=\"Portillo et al. 2019\"/>\n\n==Habitat==\nThe preferred natural [[habitat]]s of ''P. christyi'' are [[forest]] and [[savanna]], at altitudes of {{convert|600|–|1,700|m|ft|abbr=on}}.<ref name=iucn/>\n\n==Description==\nThe [[Dorsum (anatomy)|dorsum]] of the body of ''P. christyi'' is black. The ventral surface of the head is also black. The [[Ventral scales|ventrals]] and [[Subcaudal scales|subcaudals]] are white, broadly margined with black.\n\nThe [[Type (biology)|type specimen]], a female, is {{convert|43|cm|in|frac=8|abbr=on}} in total length, which includes a tail {{convert|28|mm|in|frac=8|abbr=on}} long.\n\nThe [[dorsal scales]] are smooth, without apical pits, and are arranged in 15 rows at midbody. The ventrals number 209. The [[Anal scale|anal plate]] is divided. The subcaudals number 20, also divided.\n\nThe diameter of the eye is three fifths its distance from the mouth. The [[Rostral scale|rostral]] is higher than wide, barely visible from above. The [[Internasal scales|internasals]] are slightly shorter than the [[Prefrontal scales|prefrontals]]. The [[Frontal scale|frontal]] is slightly longer than broad, much broader than the [[Supraocular scales|supraoculars]], as long as its distance from the rostral, much shorter than the [[Parietal scales|parietals]]. The [[Nasal scale|nasal]] is entire, in contact with the [[Ocular scales|preocular]]. There are two postoculars. The [[Temporal scales|temporals]] are 1+1. There are seven [[Supralabial scale|upper labials]], the third and fourth entering the eye. There are four [[Sublabial scale|lower labials]] in contact with the anterior [[Chin shields|chin shield]], the first lower labial forming a suture with its fellow behind the [[Mental scale|mental]]. There are two pairs of chin shields, the anterior pair larger than the posterior pair.<ref name=Blgr1903/>\n\n==Diet==\n''P. christyi'' [[Predation|preys]] upon snakes, including those of its own species.<ref name=iucn/>\n\n==Reproduction==\n''P. christyi'' is [[Oviparity|oviparous]].<ref name=RDB/>\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist|refs=\n<ref name=\"Portillo et al. 2019\">{{cite journal |last1=Portillo |first1=Frank |author-link=species:Frank Portillo |last2=Branch |first2=William R. |author2-link=William Roy Branch |last3=Tilbury |first3=Colin R. |author3-link=species:Colin R. Tilbury |last4=Nagy |first4=Zoltán T. |author4-link=species:Zoltán Tamás Nagy |last5=Hughes |first5=Daniel F. |author5-link=species:Daniel F. Hughes |last6=Kusamba |first6=Chifundera |author6-link=species:Chifundera Kusamba |last7=Muninga |first7=Wandege M. |author7-link=species:Wandege M. Muninga| last8=Aristote |first8=Mwenebatu M. |author8-link=species:Mwenebatu M. Aristote |last9=Behangana |first9=Mathias |author9-link=species:Mathias Behangana |last10=Greenbaum |first10=Eli |author10-link=species:Eli Greenbaum |title=A cryptic new species of ''Polemon'' (Squamata: Lamprophiidae, Aparallactinae) from the miombo woodlands of Central and East Africa |journal=Copeia |date=2019 |volume=107 |issue=1 |pages=22–35 |doi=10.1643/CH-18-098|doi-access=free }}</ref>\n}}\n\n==Further reading==\n*[[species:Stephen Spawls|Spawls S]], [[species:Kim Monroe Howell|Howell K]], [[species:Harald Hinkel|Hinkel H]], [[species:Michele Menegon|Menegon M]] (2018). ''Field Guide to East African Reptiles, Second Edition''. London: Bloomsbury Natural History. 624 pp. {{ISBN|978-1472935618}}. (''Polemon christyi'', p. 461).\n*[[species:Colin R. Tilbury|Tilbury, Colin]], [[William Roy Branch|Branch, Bill]] (2014). \"''Polemon christyi'' (Boulenger, 1903) Christy's Snake-eater\". ''African Herp News'' (61): 36–38.\n\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q3060996}}\n\n[[Category:Atractaspididae]]\n[[Category:Snakes of Africa]]\n[[Category:Reptiles of the Democratic Republic of the Congo]]\n[[Category:Reptiles of Kenya]]\n[[Category:Reptiles of South Sudan]]\n[[Category:Reptiles of Uganda]]\n[[Category:Reptiles described in 1903]]\n[[Category:Taxa named by George Albert Boulenger]]"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-10-30T05:19:35Z","lastrevid":1355030157,"length":6787}]}}